    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests passing, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a structured address form to the `POST /api/owners` create pipeline while keeping the flat `address` input fully backward-compatible.\n\n**Contract (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)**\n- Added optional `addressLine1` and optional `addressLine2` to the `OwnerFields` schema (so both the request and response DTOs carry them).\n- Removed `address` from the schema's `required` list \u2014 a structured request supplies its address via `addressLine1` instead, so earlier minimal owners and new structured owners are both accepted.\n\n**Validation & normalization (`ValidateOwnerFields.java`)**\n- Normalizes whichever address fields are supplied (`addressLine1`, `addressLine2`, and/or flat `address`) via the existing `AddressNormalizer` (trim/collapse/upper-case, `ST\u2192STREET` etc.).\n- Prefers the structured form: when `addressLine1` is non-blank, it composes the flat `address` as the normalized `addressLine1`, with a single space and the normalized `addressLine2` appended only when the second line is present.\n- Requires an address in *either* form: the `address` field is non-blank after composition (from structured) or from the flat input, plus `city`/`firstName`/`lastName`/`telephone` as before.\n\n**Persistence**\n- Added `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` columns to the `Owner` entity and to all four DB schemas (`hsqldb` \u2014 used by the tests \u2014 plus `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`). The composed value continues to live in `address`, so the household hash, postcode validation and locality (all keyed on `city`/`postcode` and the stored `address`) see the structured value.\n- `ApplyOwner` (the PUT path) now also copies the structured fields so updates persist them.\n\nBecause the composed string is stored in `address`, everything downstream that reads the address sees the structured value when present and falls back to the flat input otherwise. MapStruct auto-maps the new fields by name in both directions, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns both `addressLine1` and the composed `address` \u2014 exactly what the new acceptance test asserts (`\"10 KING STREET\"` for each).",
